 "pg_test_fsync_raw": "5 seconds per test\nO_DIRECT supported on this platform for open_datasync and open_sync.\n\nCompare file sync methods using one 8kB write:\n(in \"wal_sync_method\" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)\n        open_datasync                      4962.952 ops/sec     201 usecs/op\n        fdatasync                          5135.125 ops/sec     195 usecs/op\n        fsync                              4358.595 ops/sec     229 usecs/op\n        fsync_writethrough                              n/a\n        open_sync                          4524.329 ops/sec     221 usecs/op\n\nCompare file sync methods using two 8kB writes:\n(in \"wal_sync_method\" preference order, except fdatasync is Linux's default)\n        open_datasync                      4730.894 ops/sec     211 usecs/op\n        fdatasync                          3889.934 ops/sec     257 usecs/op\n        fsync                              3452.107 ops/sec     290 usecs/op\n        fsync_writethrough                              n/a\n        open_sync                          3214.347 ops/sec     311 usecs/op\n\nCompare open_sync with different write sizes:\n(This is designed to compare the cost of writing 16kB in different write\nopen_sync sizes.)\n         1 * 16kB open_sync write          3513.935 ops/sec     285 usecs/op\n         2 *  8kB open_sync writes         4057.233 ops/sec     246 usecs/op\n         4 *  4kB open_sync writes         2735.795 ops/sec     366 usecs/op\n         8 *  2kB open_sync writes          819.591 ops/sec    1220 usecs/op\n        16 *  1kB open_sync writes          283.984 ops/sec    3521 usecs/op\n\nTest if fsync on non-write file descriptor is honored:\n(If the times are similar, fsync() can sync data written on a different\ndescriptor.)\n        write, fsync, close                2909.477 ops/sec     344 usecs/op\n        write, close, fsync                3150.083 ops/sec     317 usecs/op\n\nNon-sync'ed 8kB writes:\n        write                             52525.505 ops/sec      19 usecs/op\n",
